menu "Robot Buddy face"

    choice FACE_TRANSPORT
        prompt "Pi link transport"
        default FACE_TRANSPORT_USB
        help
            How the face talks to the Pi. Both carry the same COBS protocol.
            See docs/face-uart-transport.md.

        config FACE_TRANSPORT_USB
            bool "USB CDC on the side USB-C (bench)"
        config FACE_TRANSPORT_UART
            bool "UART0 on the P2 connector (in the robot)"
            help
                GPIO43 TX / GPIO44 RX to the Pi's GPIO15 / GPIO14. TinyUSB is not
                started, so the USB-C port stays the chip's USB-Serial/JTAG and
                `idf.py flash` works over it with auto-reset.
    endchoice

    config FACE_UART_BAUD
        int "UART link baud rate"
        depends on FACE_TRANSPORT_UART
        default 115200
        help
            Must match the supervisor's face baud rate.

endmenu
